ZakkeN Project – Library Guide for AI
This project uses Rust libraries exposed to Android via UniFFI. The main ones:

z_db: SQLite database wrapper (db_wrapper)
protocol: data types (records, enums) and serialization
client_table_blueprints: table schemas and row creation helpers
yrs: Yrs CRDT wrappers for page content and sync
love_letter: edit contract types and serialization for client–server communication
text_diff: character-level diffing logic for text editing

Kotlin generated bindings:
com.z_db.android_mascot (from db_wrapper)
uniffi.protocol (from protocol)
rustlib.client_table_blueprints (from client_table_blueprints)
rustlib.my_yrs_lib (from yrs)
rustlib.love_letter (from love_letter)
rustlib.text_diff (from text_diff)

Core database object: LiveForever
Methods include: create_table, create_foreign_table, list_tables, get_data, get_data_ordered, insert_data, drop_table, edit_col_in_row, check_table, delete_row, swap_columns, create_index, check_index, add_column, remove_column, export_database, export_tables, create_table_from_export, copy_table.

Use `awaitReady()` before calling DB methods in UI components to ensure initialization is complete.

Important types (from protocol):
Col: Null, Integer(i64), Real(f64), Text(String), Blob(Vec<u8>)
Row: contains Vec<Col>
GetDataIn: table_name, arguments (SelectArgument), columns_to_read
InsertDataIn: table_name, values (Vec<ColumnValue>)
EditColInRowIn: table_name, row_id, column, new_value (Col)

Table blueprints (client_table_blueprints):
pages: page_id, blobbed_page, page_status, version, is_main_menu_page
backlinks: page_that_holds_link_id, page_being_linked_to_id, disabled, version
every_block_in_existence: title, page_that_owns_me, content, my_id_as_given_by_yrs, id_of_page_i_belong_to
uncommitted_diffs: snapshot_of_edit, love_letter_sketch, session_id, target_id
key_value_storage: key, value

Row creation helpers:
new_page_row(page_id, is_main_menu_page, user_id)
new_backlink_row(owner, target)
new_key_value_item(key, value)
new_every_block_in_existence_row(title, content, my_id_as_given_by_yrs, id_of_page_i_belong_to)

Yrs library:
BossOfYrs: main page document (insert/delete blocks, edit text, snapshot, merge)
YrsActivePages: mark pages active/deleted, snapshot
YrsBacklinks: disabled flag, snapshot, bookmark

LoveLetter library:
Defines the contract for how the client describes an edit so the server knows how to apply it.
Main types:
LoveLetterSketch – describes the user’s intent (without the snapshot). Variants:
EditBlock { text_edit, edit_target, target_page_id }
CreateNewBlock { position_to_insert, target_page_id }
RemoveBlock { position, target_page_id }
DisablePage { page_id }
CreateNewPage { page_id }

Important functions:
build_a_love_letter(sketch: LoveLetterSketch, snapshot: Vec<u8>) -> LoveLetter
sketch_to_bytes(sketch: &LoveLetterSketch) -> Result<Vec<u8>, BrokenHeart>
deserialize_sketch(bytes: Vec<u8>) -> Result<LoveLetterSketch, BrokenHeart>
love_letter_to_bytes(letter: &LoveLetter) -> Result<Vec<u8>, BrokenHeart>
deserialize_love_letter(bytes: Vec<u8>) -> Result<LoveLetter, BrokenHeart>

Android side:
DbManager (singleton) holds a LiveForever instance.
StorageAccess/StorageInitializer manage key_value_storage (user_id, session_id, current_document).
FastStorage provides a whitelisted in-memory cache for high-frequency StorageKeys.
SessionManager manages a thread-safe, persistent session counter incremented on launch and navigation.

Enforced Integrity Suite (z.zndroid.Tests):
These tests are production-set and can be run in-app or via Gradle build (`./gradlew test`).
The build FAILs if any test in RegisterTests fails.
ExpectedSchema: The "Ground Truth" defining what Kotlin expects.
SchemaSyncTest: Detects drift between Kotlin code, Rust blueprints, and SQLite.
PageDataSyncTest: programmatically verifies that all SQLite block data matches the Yrs CRDT blobs.

Document Events (z.zndroid.DocEvents):
AddBlock: insert new block and persist to both data and sync tables.
EditTextInBlock: updates text/meta using text_diff to generate Yrs TextEdit.
RemoveBlock: deletes block from CRDT and SQLite.
CheckIfTablesInSync: utility to compare SQLite row content vs CRDT blob content.

Common patterns:
Create tables with CreateTableIn + column defs from blueprints.
Insert rows: map cols to ColumnValue (skip auto-increment id column).
For uncommitted edits: store serialized LoveLetterSketch in love_letter_sketch and Yrs diff in snapshot_of_edit.

